NAME
    ssh-askpass - OpenSSH askpass companion for ssh.lib.sh

SYNOPSIS
    ssh-askpass

DESCRIPTION
    ssh-askpass is the bootstrap-integrated helper used by ssh.lib.sh.
    It reads the invocation-owned one-shot IPC value identified by
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID and writes that value for OpenSSH.

    Normal callers use ssh_password from ssh.lib.sh rather than invoking this
    command directly.

ENVIRONMENT
    m_SSH_ASKPASS_ID
        Required one-shot IPC identity established by ssh.lib.sh.

EXIT STATUS
    0   value delivered successfully
    1   missing or invalid IPC identity, or IPC delivery failure
    2   command arguments were supplied

SEE ALSO
    ssh.lib.sh
    ipc.lib.sh
